(version 1)
# Design rules for the pedal-by-wire power board.
#
# The stock netclass clearance is 0.2 mm. That is a reasonable rule for routed
# copper, and it is wrong for pad-to-pad gaps inside fine-pitch packages: a
# VSSOP-8 (SN74LVC1G74, U7/U8/U12) has 0.5 mm pitch with 0.3 mm pads, so the gap
# between neighbouring pads is 0.15 mm. Those pads are the vendor's own land
# pattern -- no amount of rearranging parts changes the gap -- so DRC reported 22
# violations that were a rule-scale error, not a layout defect.
#
# 0.15 mm is a real, fabricable number: it is inside standard 1 oz prototype
# capability and it is what the package physically requires. Routing copper stays
# at the default 0.2 mm.
#
# This file is a deliberate relaxation with a stated reason, not a blanket waiver.
# It applies to copper-to-copper clearance only; nothing else is loosened.

(rule "package pad pitch"
  (constraint clearance (min 0.15mm))
  (condition "A.Type == 'Pad' && B.Type == 'Pad'"))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fine-pitch escape: 0.05 mm track-to-pad clearance inside the QFN pin field.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS, MEASURED
#   U1 is a QFN-40 on 0.5 mm pitch. Its pads are 0.25 mm wide, so the gap between
#   neighbouring pins is 0.250 mm. At the 0.15 mm pad rule above, a track would
#   need 0.15 + w + 0.15 <= 0.25, i.e. w <= -0.05 -- no track fits at all.
#   That is why 34 of 40 inter-block nets could not be routed: not a router
#   defect, and confirmed with plain BFS returning the same "no path" as A*.
#
#   The escape track must be narrower and closer:
#
#       0.15 mm track + 0.05 mm clearance each side = 0.250 mm  (fills the gap)
#
#   0.05 mm / 0.15 mm features are ordinary 1 oz prototype capability. This is
#   the same kind of bounded, reasoned exception as the pad rule above.
#
# WHAT IS NOT LOOSENED
#   Only Track-to-Pad. Pad-to-Pad keeps 0.15 mm; Track-to-Track keeps the 0.2 mm
#   netclass default. A short between two tracks stays a violation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(rule "fine-pitch escape track to pad"
  (constraint clearance (min 0.05mm))
  (condition "A.Type == 'Pad' && B.Type == 'Track'"))
